  "body": "### What should we add?\n\nThe [`solve_fermion`](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-addon-sqd/blob/eedfcf980fb3ead067201b24ca169ccb36019f9e/qiskit_addon_sqd/fermion.py#L72) function accepts an array of bitstrings, where each bitstring has an \"alpha\" half and a \"beta\" half. In order to form the actual SCI subspace, these bitstrings are split into alpha and beta halves (this is done in [`bitstring_matrix_to_ci_strs`](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-addon-sqd/blob/eedfcf980fb3ead067201b24ca169ccb36019f9e/qiskit_addon_sqd/fermion.py#L399)) and the actual subspace is formed as the cross product of the sets of unique alpha strings and unique beta strings. Furthermore, for closed-shell systems, the alpha and beta sets are actually merged, and the subspace formed as the cross product of the merged set with itself.\n\nThis procedure makes it difficult to directly control the subspace dimension, which is a useful feature. I'm not sure what we should do. Perhaps in hindsight, we should not have deprecated the [option](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-addon-sqd/blob/eedfcf980fb3ead067201b24ca169ccb36019f9e/qiskit_addon_sqd/fermion.py#L114-L120) to pass the CI strings directly as input.",
